From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 23:30:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvk: NVK_PASS_PROFILE times work outside render passes, more
 signatures

The CS2 capture with patch 0010 explained only 45 % of the GPU time: about
550 of 990 GPU ms/s was in no render pass, and the 128-entry signature
table had filled up with signatures from the map load, so about 4900
passes a second were dropped (the logged count was cumulative, which hid
how many per window).

Operations outside render passes are now timed as runs of one kind:
dispatches, indirect dispatches, buffer copies, image copies, buffer to
image and image to buffer copies, fills, updates, colour and depth/stencil
image clears, blits, vkCmdResolveImage, the resolve at the end of a render
pass, query resets and query copies.  A run ends at the next render pass,
operation of another kind, secondary or the end of the command buffer, so
it includes the barriers between its operations.  Meta operations and the
render passes the driver records itself (image clears, resolves, ZCULL
reseeds) count towards the operation that records them instead of showing
up as passes of their own.  Each report goes to the engine of the last
method: the 3D class as before, the compute class after WAIT_FOR_IDLE, or
the copy engine with a non-pipelined semaphore, so a copy's or dispatch's
time is its own.

Every window now logs a summary: command buffers = render passes +
operations + the time between them (barriers, state, waits), the GPU time
of each operation kind with its rate, and the 40 heaviest signatures.

Each line now also says, per instance, the draw calls, the draws they make
(vkCmdDrawMulti*EXT and indirect multi-draws count drawCount, indirect
count draws maxDrawCount), the indirect calls and draws, queries begun and
pipeline barriers.  "Draws" in 0010 counted calls only, which hides DXVK's
batching of D3D11 draws into multi-draws and of DrawIndexedInstancedIndirect
runs into one vkCmdDrawIndexedIndirect.  Render pass signatures also carry
the load and store ops of the first colour and the depth attachment and
whether the depth image has ZCULL storage.

NVK_PASS_PROFILE=2 adds, per render pass, the vertex shader, clipper in
and out and fragment shader invocation counters and the four ZCULL
statistics counters (raw deltas).

Capacity: 4096 signatures (hash lookup instead of a linear strcmp), 65536
ring slots, dropped signatures counted per window.  The harvest thread no
longer holds the recording threads' lock while it scans the ring.
